description:
Line 977-983:
```rust
let full_window = bitmap == required && bitmap.count_ones() == regular_count as u32;
let ack_bitmap = if full_window && regular_count > 1 {
    bitmap
} else {
    bitmap | 1
};
```

When `regular_count == 1` and MIC fails with all fragments present, the code sets bit 0 (marks All-1 as received) rather than requesting All-1 retransmission.

Scenario:
1. Window has 1 regular fragment (FCN=62) + All-1
2. Both received, MIC check fails
3. `regular_count = 1`, `full_window = true`
4. But `regular_count > 1` is false, so `ack_bitmap = bitmap | 1`
5. All-1 is marked received, only regular fragment retransmitted
6. Retransmitting the regular fragment will not fix the MIC

The comment on lines 971-976 explains the intent but the `regular_count > 1` condition may be too restrictive.

Suggested fix: Review whether `regular_count > 1` should be `regular_count >= 1` or if single-fragment windows need different handling.
